{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1474341-changeling-in-the-balkans","id":1474341,"title":"Changeling in...the Balkans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-09T17:48:36-08:00","id":1474341,"title":"Changeling in...the Balkans?","content":"I was reviewing the list of different Kingdoms in C20 and out of amusement, I noticed that none of the different polities like the Galician Confederation, Empire of the Caucaus, Kingdom of Hellas, or Kingdom of the Firebird could notably lay claim to the Balkans: Albania, Bulgaria, and the former Yugoslavian territories appear to be, for all intents and purposes, terra nullius. (Though not technically Balkan, you could arguably discuss Romania and Moldova here as well)<br /> <br /> While there was an earlier Reddit post joking about a &quot;missing duchy&quot; in Concordia (&quot;we don't talk about the Lost Troll Kingdom of Minnesota&quot;), this seems like a much larger absence.<br /> <br /> Potentially, this situation could be handled as follows:<br /> The lands of the Balkans were laid claim to by the nobles of the nearby Kingdoms during the The Accordance War. However, territorial ambiguities combined with covert material aid from the Galician Confederation has left the Balkans a sort of &quot;neutral zone/no man's land&quot; where there is no de-facto leadership council.<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could just make a politics joke about the Sidhe coming back during the Resurgence, seeing all the concrete bunkers dotting Albania, and deciding the place was too banal for them.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how &quot;the Balkans&quot; are integrated into Changeling society as a whole, there's also the intersection with real-world politics. After all, for all their issues, the 60s and early 70s were a relatively &quot;stable&quot; period for the Balkans. They were all socialist/communist though all ideologically distinct, with Bulgaria in the Soviet Bloc, Yugoslavia nonaligned, and Albania akin to Europe's North Korea...<br /> <br /> ...of course, come the fall of the USSR and Communism in general, as well as the breakup of Yugoslavia. Said conflict drew in extremists from every side, with Neonazis, militant Orthodox paramilitaries, and mujahdeen all piling in to aid the factions they felt represented their respective warped causes...<br /> <br /> And this is just on the mortal side! <br /> <br /> Is it a compelling enough backdrop for what is otherwise a rather messy time-period in history?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T21:10:10-08:00","id":1474351,"title":"","content":"If memory fails me not, much of the region is also strongly associated in WoD with a centuries - if not millenia-long - ongoing conflict between the Tzimisce and Shadow Lords, with some Gangrel, Nosferatu &amp; Tremere boxed in? I can see that, along with Kupala-related things, turn into extra complications to push interest for the area from lords just arrived from Arcadia in the 70s way down indeed.<br /> <br /> All of that said, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Rage_Across_Russia\" target=\"_blank\">Rage Across Russia</a> has a number of spirits inspired on its folklore that might serve as decent inspiration for kiths or other Dreaming natives present in at least the slavic languages-speaking parts of the region, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-10-2022, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T23:37:27-08:00","id":1474354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1474341-changeling-in-the-balkans?p=1474351#post1474351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of that said, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Rage_Across_Russia\" target=\"_blank\">Rage Across Russia</a> has a number of spirits inspired on its folklore that might serve as decent inspiration for kiths or other Dreaming natives present in at least the slavic languages-speaking parts of the region, i guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of Lost Houses has a sidebar in the Varich chapter on Russian inanimae, which might also serve as inspiration in that regard.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T03:15:15-08:00","id":1474361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1474341-changeling-in-the-balkans?p=1474354#post1474354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Book of Lost Houses has a sidebar in the Varich chapter on Russian inanimae, which might also serve as inspiration in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good - and as an aside i wouldn't be surprised if there was some degree of mix-up with some folkloric beings appearing as either or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T09:45:51-08:00","id":1474743,"title":"","content":"There are some 'distinctly' &quot;South Slav&quot; fairies that could either exist as variants of other pre-established kith as well. Among the more notable ones is the Vila.<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vila_(fairy\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vila_(fairy</a>)<br /> <br /> And yes, if these sound somehow familiar, these are what the Veela in Harry Potter are based off of.<br /> <br /> Other distinctly &quot;South Slav/Balkan&quot; options include:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ved_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ved_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\"> Ved (mythology) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ved_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ved_(mythology) </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samodiva_(folklore\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samodiva_(folklore</a>)<br /> <br /> Given the &quot;cultural crossroads/intersection&quot; of this territory, odds are you're going to see at least several &quot;western&quot; Kithain, including Strega, Satyrs, the odd Troll born of gastarbeiter descendants of the Danube Swabians, at least a few Middle Eastern Kithain from the C20 Player's Guide, etc.<br /> <br /> In that regard, it could debatably be less about being 'terra nullius', and more just being an 'undecided territory' given the regional volatility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T22:52:22-08:00","id":1475193,"title":"","content":"I think the 'undecided' approach works best given the regions both actual and fictional history. The local Commoners could already act as representatives/proxies for the SL/Tz conflict, if not directly at least mirroring its themes. It would make sense that the Sidhe find there a place where there are already groups in conflict, with enough outside back-up to not be simple to overthrow or try as they did elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}